        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1fc53ae0-e3e9-5283-85ed-f35b102a0fbd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Arnold, Raymond A. Palmer\n- Events: World UFO Day, 1947 Roswell UFO Incident\n- Places: Mount Rainier, Washington, United States\n- Products: The Coming of the Saucers, Mystic, Search, Flying Saucers\n- Concepts: unidentified flying objects, flying saucers\n\nFacts:\n- On June 24, 1947, Kenneth Arnold claimed to see nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington.\n- Kenneth Arnold's June 24, 1947 sighting is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- July 2 is observed by World UFO Day to commemorate the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\n- June 24 is observed by World UFO Day because it marks Kenneth Arnold's widely reported unidentified flying object sighting.\n- Raymond A. Palmer published magazines including Mystic, Search, and Flying Saucers.\n- Raymond A. Palmer co-wrote The Coming of the Saucers with Kenneth Arnold, and the book was related to flying saucers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7da77708-2b10-5736-84be-1de85038c529",
        "text": "Page: World UFO Day. Sentence: June 24 is the date that aviator Kenneth Arnold reported what is generally considered to be the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, while July 2 commemorates the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\nPage: Kenneth Arnold. Sentence: He is best known for making what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, after claiming to have seen nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington on June 24, 1947.\nPage: Raymond A. Palmer. Sentence: In addition to magazines such as \"Mystic,\" \"Search,\" and 'Flying Saucers,\" he published numerous spirtualist books, including \"\", as well as several books related to flying saucers, including \"The Coming of the Saucers,\" co-written by Palmer with Kenneth Arnold.",
